WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.427 --> 00:00:07.510
(laughs)

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.453
(speaks in Italian)

00:00:13.453 --> 00:00:14.550
- My name is Simone Falco.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.123
I'm the chef/owner of Rossopomodaro.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.790
I've been making pizzas
since I was very young.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.560
I'm very excited today,
because we're gonna

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.360
discover which one is the best

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.120
delivery pizza you can get at home.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:24.953
Stay tuned.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.290
Let's see what we have here.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.550
Feels super soft, and a little oily.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.383
A lot of flour underneath.

00:00:36.383 --> 00:00:38.573
That's burnt, that's why
the color is so dark.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.773
What are these?

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.606
Maybe potatoes?

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.990
There's a gooey line right in the middle,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.923
but looks pretty good.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.220
Sweet is the first thing that comes.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.680
The tomato sauce, not bad.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:50.710
There's a sauce on the side.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.403
There's a lot of butter.

00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:54.720
It's a garlic hollandaise?

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.873
Maybe dip in there?

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.410
It's having a pizza with mayonnaise,

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.340
and maybe some people like it.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.063
I don't really enjoy it, but
I guess it's a good start.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.523
Wow, we have the pepperoni.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.123
Not bad.

00:01:12.123 --> 00:01:13.810
The underneath part is cooked much better.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.563
They might use oil or
butter to make it crispy.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.720
The smell is more of a cake,
calzone more than a pizza.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:24.103
The crust is stuffed with, not
just cheese, but mozzarella.

00:01:24.848 --> 00:01:26.210
I think the cheese of a better quality.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.513
Less sugar, less doughy.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.630
I think it's a little too soft.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.740
Not enough tomato sauce, barely a little,

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:32.760
but overall it's not bad.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.330
Pull out directly from the fridge,

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.740
get a bite before you go to bed.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.573
I would do that.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.793
Okay, definitely thinner crust.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.070
I can see oregano.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.670
The crust smells of oil.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.763
Inside is a little tight.

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:51.303
It's pretty good.

00:01:51.303 --> 00:01:52.790
I don't see sugar in the tomato sauce,

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:53.720
which makes me very happy.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.590
I don't taste the sugar into the dough,

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.620
which makes me happy again.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.340
It stays there, doesn't drip oil.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.156
This is the pizza I would
like to sit on the couch

00:02:00.156 --> 00:02:03.080
on a Sunday, watching the
football with an easy beer,

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.363
or as I prefer, the wine.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.443
It delivers.

00:02:05.443 --> 00:02:06.580
I think this is the best so far.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:07.693
This is my favorite.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.313
Oh my lord.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:16.203
This is nice.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.163
What is it?

00:02:17.163 --> 00:02:17.996
It's a pie.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.163
I see a lot of sausages, mushroom,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.803
jalapeno, uncooked dough.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.733
Dense, doughy, but the cooking
technique is much better.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:27.890
They use very good ingredients.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:30.423
The heavy weight on top tastes good,

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.253
but that part feels to me soupy.

00:02:38.165 --> 00:02:40.230
And here we are, (speaks Italian).

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:44.160
They use a little semolina
flour to make it crispier,

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.930
which will give a nice bite, a nice touch.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.110
The cooking technique is good.

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:47.943
It holds up well.

00:02:47.943 --> 00:02:51.113
A lot, a lot, a lot of
olive oil in the dough.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:52.940
Sweet, sugar back.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.100
The amount of sugar that
you feel everywhere,

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.080
for me it's too much.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.860
But overall, I guess fairly balanced.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.793
Definitely on the top rank on
the one that we tried today.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.910
The culture of pizza is
the neighbor who plays,

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.573
the family that runs it for you.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:05.503
Talk with them.

00:03:05.503 --> 00:03:08.053
Buy something more simple, and eat it hot.

00:03:08.799 --> 00:03:11.382
(upbeat music)

